{"type":"message","id":"7b938fc7","parentId":"33209f93","timestamp":"2026-05-21T08:29:07.340Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CVsCqqYAPbPw0nAVB0P2xeD8","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave Asks Arbitrum to Unfreeze Stolen Kelp DAO Funds to Contain Fallout\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365431/aave-leads-defi-united-push-to-contain-292m-kelpdao-fallout\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The unfreezing proposal asks for funds to be directed to a remediation effort called 'DeFi United' aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The overall Kelp exploit was valued at approximately $292-$293 million.\",\n    \"Aave was severely impacted by the hack, with its Total Value Locked (TVL) dropping nearly $12 billion in one week.\",\n    \"The hacker used stolen rsETH as collateral on Aave to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving behind over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave founder Stani Kulechov pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money to the recovery efforts.\",\n    \"The 'DeFi United' relief effort has already seen $21 million in contributions from various protocols (including Kelp DAO, BGD Labs, Golem Foundation, Babylon) and individuals.\",\n    \"Another $215 million has been conditionally pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido, subject to DAO governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave Labs expects the recovery effort to take roughly seven weeks (49 days) to normalize conditions for Arbitrum users and the DeFi ecosystem.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":64,"aggregated":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave Asks Arbitrum to Unfreeze Stolen Kelp DAO Funds to Contain Fallout\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365431/aave-leads-defi-united-push-to-contain-292m-kelpdao-fallout\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The unfreezing proposal asks for funds to be directed to a remediation effort called 'DeFi United' aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The overall Kelp exploit was valued at approximately $292-$293 million.\",\n    \"Aave was severely impacted by the hack, with its Total Value Locked (TVL) dropping nearly $12 billion in one week.\",\n    \"The hacker used stolen rsETH as collateral on Aave to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving behind over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave founder Stani Kulechov pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money to the recovery efforts.\",\n    \"The 'DeFi United' relief effort has already seen $21 million in contributions from various protocols (including Kelp DAO, BGD Labs, Golem Foundation, Babylon) and individuals.\",\n    \"Another $215 million has been conditionally pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido, subject to DAO governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave Labs expects the recovery effort to take roughly seven weeks (49 days) to normalize conditions for Arbitrum users and the DeFi ecosystem.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"\n}","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779352147340}}
{"type":"message","id":"723b526f","parentId":"7b938fc7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T08:29:09.243Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_WNKB6BuyDRL9xZFaQzMi4gfu","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rg -n \"chart_coin|primary_keyword|topic_theme|combined_key_facts|aggregated_raw_content|required fields\" -S /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher /tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633 | sed -n '1,200p'","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","yieldMs":1000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":1589,"output":186,"cacheRead":8832,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10607,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779352147341,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dht47UJsSjRqgceS7AIFh3g3WcAcG"}}
{"type":"message","id":"21ebed42","parentId":"723b526f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T08:29:09.691Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WNKB6BuyDRL9xZFaQzMi4gfu","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Tennessee Bans Bitcoin ATMs\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Tennessee Bitcoin ATM ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:19:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Tennessee has become the second U.S. state to outlaw Bitcoin ATMs, making it a criminal offense in the Volunteer State to own or operate the machines that federal authorities have identified as a vector committing fraud against the elderly. Whether operators’ kiosks allow customers to purchase Bitcoin or other digital assets with cash, they have until July 1 to pull the plug under House Bill 2505, which Tennessee Governor Bill Lee signed into law on April 13 following the legislation’s introduction earlier this year.\\n\\nThe legislation was co-sponsored by Republican state representatives Cameron Sexton and Jay Reedy. In a March statement, Sexton said the kiosks “have become a gateway for scammers to exploit Tennesseans, especially our seniors.” Sexton noted that victims defrauded while using Bitcoin ATMs often have little hope of recovering their money once it’s gone. That was around the time that local authorities warned of a scam where victims had lost $4 million to overseas scammers posing as law enforcement.\\n\\nReedy, a certified master beef producer, said “Crypto ATMs have given scammers a fast and easy way to target our citizens and scare them into draining their savings.” The two-page bill, which was introduced in February, classifies violations as a Class A misdemeanor, on par in Tennessee with simple drug possession and domestic assault.\\n\\nIn total, Tennessee hosts 651 Bitcoin ATMs, with a majority of them clustered around Nashville, the state’s most populous city and capital, according to Coin ATM Radar. According to FBI numbers released this month, Americans aged over 60 lost $257 million to scams involving Bitcoin ATMs last year, a 58% increase year-over-year. Citizens under 30, for comparison, lost $6.6 million to that type of scam in 2025. In March, Indiana became the first U.S. state to impose a sweeping ban on Bitcoin ATMs. Amid an uptick in scams, several states have passed legislation imposing transaction limits and mandating refunds for victims. In Minnesota, lawmakers are weighing legislation that would follow Tennessee’s lead and ban Bitcoin ATMs across the state.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:22:  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:23:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:33:  \"combined_key_facts\": key_facts,\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:34:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": raw_text[:5000] # Ensuring sufficient length\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Western Union stablecoin\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin Plus ‘Stable Card’ Next Month - Decrypt{\\n \\\"@context\\\": \\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"NewsArticle\\\",\\n \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin Plus ‘Stable Card’ Next Month\\\",\\n \\\"image\\\": [\\\"https://cdn.decrypt.co/resize/1024/height/512/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Western-Union2-gID_7.jpg\\\"],\\n \\\"datePublished\\\": \\\"2026-04-27T10:02:52\\\",\\n \\\"dateModified\\\": \\\"2026-04-27T10:02:52\\\",\\n \\\"author\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"Person\\\",\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"Decrypt Agent\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"publisher\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"Organization\\\",\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"Decrypt\\\",\\n \\\"logo\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"ImageObject\\\",\\n \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/decrypt-mark.png\\\"\\n }\\n },\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"The USDPT stablecoin launching next month will serve as an alternative to SWIFT for agent settlements rather than consumer transactions.\\\",\\n \\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\": \\\"https://decrypt.co/365593/western-union-to-launch-solana-based-stablecoin-plus-stable-card-next-month\\\",\\n \\\"articleSection\\\": \\\"News\\\",\\\"keywords\\\": \\\"Business,solana,stablecoin,western union,USDPT\\\"\\n }\\n gtag(\\\"consent\\\", \\\"default\\\", {\\n ad_personalization: \\\"denied\\\",\\n ad_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n ad_user_data: \\\"denied\\\",\\n analytics_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n functionality_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n personalization_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n security_storage: \\\"granted\\\",\\n wait_for_update: 500\\n });\\n gtag(\\\"set\\\", \\\"ads_data_redaction\\\", true);\\n gtag(\\\"set\\\", \\\"url_passthrough\\\", true);\\n Western Union CEO Devin McGranahan said the company will focus on expanding adoption and embedding digital assets into its core money movement platform going forward. The USDPT stablecoin launching next month will serve as an alternative to SWIFT for agent settlements rather than consumer transactions. A new ‘Stable Card’ will also be released.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py:8:  python3 extract_tweet_quotes.py --from-file /tmp/research.json --field aggregated_raw_content --merge-into /tmp/research.json\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py:142:    parser.add_argument(\"--field\", default=\"aggregated_raw_content\", help=\"JSON field to scan\")\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/README.md:21:  --field aggregated_raw_content \\\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to “DeFi United.” DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the “DeFi United” coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Adoption of Solana for Stablecoin Payments by Major Financial Institutions\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Solana stablecoin payments\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Due to a temporary block from1 the source, I was unable to fetch the full article text. The key facts have been extracted and are available in the `combined_key_facts` section.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"SBI Holdings' Potential Acquisition of Bitbank\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"SBI Bitbank acquisition\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n\n⚠️ [... middle content omitted — showing head and tail ...]\n\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:133:**Do NOT append anything after the closing `}`. The `chart_coin` field inside the JSON replaces the old separate CHART_COIN line.**\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:139:- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:142:- Never fabricate X/Twitter posts or tweet URLs. If articles link to `x.com/.../status/...`, include those URLs in `aggregated_raw_content`; do not make up tweet text.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:143:- `primary_keyword`, `primary_asset`, and `chart_coin` in your JSON are derived from the **chosen story**, not from the RSS search keywords. Use the correct CoinGecko id for the main asset (e.g. `ethereum`, `solana`, `bitcoin`, `ripple` for XRP).\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"[... 48694 more characters truncated]"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":335,"aggregated":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Tennessee Bans Bitcoin ATMs\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Tennessee Bitcoin ATM ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/topic_research.json:19:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Tennessee has become the second U.S. state to outlaw Bitcoin ATMs, making it a criminal offense in the Volunteer State to own or operate the machines that federal authorities have identified as a vector committing fraud against the elderly. Whether operators’ kiosks allow customers to purchase Bitcoin or other digital assets with cash, they have until July 1 to pull the plug under House Bill 2505, which Tennessee Governor Bill Lee signed into law on April 13 following the legislation’s introduction earlier this year.\\n\\nThe legislation was co-sponsored by Republican state representatives Cameron Sexton and Jay Reedy. In a March statement, Sexton said the kiosks “have become a gateway for scammers to exploit Tennesseans, especially our seniors.” Sexton noted that victims defrauded while using Bitcoin ATMs often have little hope of recovering their money once it’s gone. That was around the time that local authorities warned of a scam where victims had lost $4 million to overseas scammers posing as law enforcement.\\n\\nReedy, a certified master beef producer, said “Crypto ATMs have given scammers a fast and easy way to target our citizens and scare them into draining their savings.” The two-page bill, which was introduced in February, classifies violations as a Class A misdemeanor, on par in Tennessee with simple drug possession and domestic assault.\\n\\nIn total, Tennessee hosts 651 Bitcoin ATMs, with a majority of them clustered around Nashville, the state’s most populous city and capital, according to Coin ATM Radar. According to FBI numbers released this month, Americans aged over 60 lost $257 million to scams involving Bitcoin ATMs last year, a 58% increase year-over-year. Citizens under 30, for comparison, lost $6.6 million to that type of scam in 2025. In March, Indiana became the first U.S. state to impose a sweeping ban on Bitcoin ATMs. Amid an uptick in scams, several states have passed legislation imposing transaction limits and mandating refunds for victims. In Minnesota, lawmakers are weighing legislation that would follow Tennessee’s lead and ban Bitcoin ATMs across the state.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:22:  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:23:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:33:  \"combined_key_facts\": key_facts,\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py:34:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": raw_text[:5000] # Ensuring sufficient length\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Western Union stablecoin\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/western_union_stablecoin.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin Plus ‘Stable Card’ Next Month - Decrypt{\\n \\\"@context\\\": \\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"NewsArticle\\\",\\n \\\"headline\\\": \\\"Western Union to Launch Solana-Based Stablecoin Plus ‘Stable Card’ Next Month\\\",\\n \\\"image\\\": [\\\"https://cdn.decrypt.co/resize/1024/height/512/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Western-Union2-gID_7.jpg\\\"],\\n \\\"datePublished\\\": \\\"2026-04-27T10:02:52\\\",\\n \\\"dateModified\\\": \\\"2026-04-27T10:02:52\\\",\\n \\\"author\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"Person\\\",\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"Decrypt Agent\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"publisher\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"Organization\\\",\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"Decrypt\\\",\\n \\\"logo\\\": {\\n \\\"@type\\\": \\\"ImageObject\\\",\\n \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://decrypt.co/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/decrypt-mark.png\\\"\\n }\\n },\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"The USDPT stablecoin launching next month will serve as an alternative to SWIFT for agent settlements rather than consumer transactions.\\\",\\n \\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\": \\\"https://decrypt.co/365593/western-union-to-launch-solana-based-stablecoin-plus-stable-card-next-month\\\",\\n \\\"articleSection\\\": \\\"News\\\",\\\"keywords\\\": \\\"Business,solana,stablecoin,western union,USDPT\\\"\\n }\\n gtag(\\\"consent\\\", \\\"default\\\", {\\n ad_personalization: \\\"denied\\\",\\n ad_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n ad_user_data: \\\"denied\\\",\\n analytics_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n functionality_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n personalization_storage: \\\"denied\\\",\\n security_storage: \\\"granted\\\",\\n wait_for_update: 500\\n });\\n gtag(\\\"set\\\", \\\"ads_data_redaction\\\", true);\\n gtag(\\\"set\\\", \\\"url_passthrough\\\", true);\\n Western Union CEO Devin McGranahan said the company will focus on expanding adoption and embedding digital assets into its core money movement platform going forward. The USDPT stablecoin launching next month will serve as an alternative to SWIFT for agent settlements rather than consumer transactions. A new ‘Stable Card’ will also be released.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py:8:  python3 extract_tweet_quotes.py --from-file /tmp/research.json --field aggregated_raw_content --merge-into /tmp/research.json\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py:142:    parser.add_argument(\"--field\", default=\"aggregated_raw_content\", help=\"JSON field to scan\")\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/README.md:21:  --field aggregated_raw_content \\\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic_news.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to “DeFi United.” DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the “DeFi United” coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Adoption of Solana for Stablecoin Payments by Major Financial Institutions\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Solana stablecoin payments\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/out.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Due to a temporary block from1 the source, I was unable to fetch the full article text. The key facts have been extracted and are available in the `combined_key_facts` section.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"SBI Holdings' Potential Acquisition of Bitbank\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"SBI Bitbank acquisition\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json:18:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 11:17:45 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nTokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary, extending its push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan as the country moves toward securities-style rules for digital assets.\\n\\nThe financial conglomerate [said](https://www.sbigroup.co.jp/news/2026/0501_16298.html) Friday it is considering a share acquisition as part of a potential capital and business alliance with Bitbank. The deal remains subject to due diligence, negotiations and internal approvals, SBI said.\\n\\nThe talks come a month after SBI VC Trade [absorbed](https://www.sbivc.co.jp/newsview/umhk6419ku) Bitpoint Japan on April 1, with SBI VC Trade becoming the surviving company. A Bitbank acquisition would give SBI a larger position in Japan’s crypto exchange market at a time when policymakers are preparing to bring crypto assets under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act.\\n\\nSBI said the potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry,” citing Japan’s planned regulatory shift for crypto assets.\\n\\nJapan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to [amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-approves-bill-classify-cryptocurrencies-financial-instruments) and the Payment Services Act, according to the Financial Services Agency. The bill is intended to strengthen market fairness, transparency and investor protection while revising rules for crypto assets.\\n\\nCrypto assets are currently regulated by the FSA under the Payment Services Act as a means of payment. The proposed changes would move crypto closer to Japan’s traditional financial market framework, with stronger disclosure, exchange oversight and rules targeting unfair trading.\\n\\nCointelegraph asked SBI Holdings for comment on the proposed Bitbank acquisition and how Japan’s shifting crypto rules are affecting the group’s exchange strategy, but had not received a response by publication.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-222.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Bitbank company profile. Source: SBI Group_\\n\\nBitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges. It [ranks](https://www.coingecko.com/en/exchanges/country/japan) as Japan’s leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score, which measures the legitimacy of crypto exchanges based on liquidity, trading activity, cybersecurity and operational scale.\\n\\nIt ranks third among cryptocurrency exchanges by daily trading volume, behind bitFlyer and Coincheck.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-223.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Top Japanese crypto exchanges by trust score. Source: Coingecko_\\n\\nThe proposed deal would add to SBI’s broader digital asset footprint. SBI made a $50 million investment in Circle's IPO in June 2025. In previous years, SBI also made strategic investments in other crypto-native companies, including BITPoint Japan, Sygnum Bank and crypto exchange TaoTao, which later merged into SBI VC Trade.\\n\\n## Japan brings crypto under TradFi umbrella, targets ETFs by 2028\\n\\nJapan’s regulatory shift comes as institutional interest in digital assets continues to grow and policymakers reassess how crypto should fit within the country’s financial markets.\\n\\nJapanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama first [signaled](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-crypto-securities-framework-exchange-led-access-2026) the intent to bring crypto under the same umbrella as traditional finance assets in January, to ensure that citizens will “benefit from digital and blockchain-based assets.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**South Korea’s Shinhan Card taps Solana to test real-world stablecoin payments**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korean-credit-card-giant-partners-with-solana-for-stablecoin-payments-defi-infrastructure)\\n\\nThe country is also planning to legalize the launch of cryptocurrency exchange-traded funds (ETFs) by 2028, [according](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-considers-crypto-etfs-2028-nikkei) to a January report. Large financial conglomerates like SBI Holdings and Nomura are among the first companies expected to [develop crypto-linked ETFs](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-plans-bitcoin-xrp-etf-japan).\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Singapore isn’t a ‘crypto hub’ — it’s something better: StraitsX CEO**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/singapore-crypto-speculation-down-mas-loophole-closure-asia-express/)\\n\\nCointelegraph\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Kelp DAO Exploit and DeFi United Recovery Effort\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Kelp DAO recovery\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single_topic.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Lending platform Aave has raised about $160 million it needs to cover the $200 million in bad debt left behind by the year's largest decentralized finance (DeFi) exploit, Arkham posted on X on Saturday. Last week, Aave and several major crypto firms announced a coordinated recovery effort to stabilize DeFi markets after a $292 million security breach left the crypto borrowing sector's largest lender facing a financial crisis. Called DeFi United and led by Aave service providers, the effort’s goal is to restore support for rsETH, the yield-bearing derivative token of ether (ETH) at the core of the exploit. The exploit is traced back to a KelpDAO integration vulnerability with LayerZero, where an attacker minted 116,500 unbacked rsETH tokens. That left Aave with impaired collateral, triggering a run on deposits as lenders rushed to exit, ultimately withdrawing $10 billion. Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether tied to the Kelp DAO attack and to direct those funds to ‘DeFi United,’ a fund aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council moved to freeze 30,765 Ether (ETH) held in a wallet connected to the $293 million Kelp exploit. The submission was made with the support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi and Compound, four of the several crypto protocols affected by the hack. Dune Analytics data shows that about $21 million in contributions has already been made, with contributions including those from Aave Labs CEO Stani Kulechov, Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, and others. Another $215 million has been pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi and Lido to assist the recovery effort, which are subject to governance votes. Aave was hit hard by the Kelp DAO exploit, with its total value locked falling nearly $12 billion in a week, leaving more than $190 million in bad debt.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/output.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Surging April Crypto Hacks Lead to Massive Losses\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/output.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Crypto Hacks April 2026\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/output.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/output.json:18:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The cryptocurrency industry has seen a sharp spike in hacks in April, with losses topping $600 million in the worst month for crypto hacks in more than a year. According to DeFiLlama, the total value hacked in April so far amounted to $629.7 million, the highest since $1.47 billion in February 2025. With KelpDAO’s $293 million hack and Drift Protocol’s $280 million exploit accounting for 82% of the monthly losses, decentralized finance (DeFi) has taken the unwanted crown as the most targeted sector over the past month. The concentration of losses in a handful of large DeFi incidents shows how a small number of attacks can still overwhelm broader security improvements across the sector. The causes of the hacks also revealed that the biggest risks are increasingly tied to bridges, privileged access and operational failures, rather than simple smart contract bugs alone. One of the latest attacks involved the DeFi derivatives platform Wasabi Protocol, which at the time of writing had been drained of around $5.5 million across Ethereum, Base, Blast and Berachain networks in an ongoing exploit, according to Certik. Recent attacks also include the move-to-earn crypto platform Sweat Economy, which reportedly lost $3.46 million, or about 65% of its liquidity pool, in under 30 seconds. The protocol later said stolen funds were frozen on MEXC shortly after the incident, with recovery efforts underway. Aftermath Finance, a Sui blockchain-based decentralized trading platform, was also among the recent DeFi hacks, suffering an exploit on its perpetuals platform. According to Blockaid, the attacker drained about $1.1 million in USDC across 11 transactions in roughly 36 minutes. April’s spike in crypto exploits reflects a shift toward more sophisticated, multi-stage attacks targeting offchain infrastructure rather than smart contract vulnerabilities, Yaniv Nissenboim, head of security solutions at Chainalysis, told Cointelegraph. “What connects these incidents is that well-resourced attackers are finding novel ways to exploit the seams between on-chain protocols and the offchain systems they depend on,” Nissenboim said. These entry points include compromised remote procedure call (RPC) nodes, breaches of cloud key management systems and long-running social engineering campaigns, he said. In many cases, on-chain transactions still appear fully legitimate, even as infrastructure or human-access layers are already compromised. Nissenboim said that real-time monitoring and automated safeguards are becoming critical, citing anomalies such as abnormal minting patterns and cross-chain inconsistencies that can be detected instantly. In one case, rapid detection helped prevent a second theft of roughly $95 million during the KelpDAO incident, he added. According to Standard Chartered’s analysts led by Geoffrey Kendrick, KelpDAO’s incident is a sign of DeFi’s growing resilience rather than a fatal failure for the sector. “While the recent KelpDAO theft and its impact on AAVE have raised questions around continued DeFi banking growth, we expect growth to remain on track as a maturing DeFi industry puts solutions in place to reduce vulnerabilities,” the bank said in a Wednesday research note seen by Cointelegraph.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/TOOLS.md:74:Scans `aggregated_raw_content` for `x.com/status/...` links from news articles and fetches verified tweet text. Scout does **not** invent tweets.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/TOOLS.md:82:  --field aggregated_raw_content \\\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/research_payload.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"DeFi United effort to recover KelpDAO exploit funds\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/research_payload.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO recovery\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/research_payload.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/research_payload.json:21:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether tied to the Kelp DAO attack and to direct those funds to “DeFi United,” a fund aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council moved to freeze 30,765 Ether (ETH) held in a wallet connected to the $293 million Kelp exploit. In a proposal posted Saturday on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs said directing those funds to a planned remediation effort would “restore normal conditions for Arbitrum users” and the wider ecosystem and that the Ether on Arbitrum “represents a material contribution” toward restoring the Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) token. The submission was made with the support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi and Compound, four of the several crypto protocols affected by the hack. The proposal comes days after Aave Labs and others set up the “DeFi United” on Friday in an effort to fully restore the backing of rsETH. Dune Analytics data shows that about $21 million in contributions has already been made, with contributions including those from Aave Labs CEO Stani Kulechov, Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, Web3 development platform BGD Labs and Babylon, a Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol. Another $215 million has been pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi and Lido to assist the recovery effort, which are subject to governance votes. LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation and Frax Finance have also signaled their intention to help. Aave was hit hard by the Kelp DAO exploit, with its total value locked falling nearly $12 billion in a week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on its lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving more than $190 million in bad debt and triggering a wave of withdrawals. In the Arbitrum proposal, Aave Labs said a full recovery would not only restore rsETH’s backing but also normalize conditions for its holders, liquidity providers and borrowers on Arbitrum and across the broader DeFi ecosystem. Even a “partial recovery would still meaningfully reduce the shortfall,” Aave Labs added. Aave Labs has specifically asked for the 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO and blockchain security platform Certora. Aave Labs said it expects the effort to restore rsETH and compensate its holders to take about 49 days and that it would return the funds if the recovery effort falls through.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json:21:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\n[](https://www.coindesk.com/)\\n*   News \\n*   Video \\n*   [Prices](https://www.coindesk.com/price)\\n*   [Research](https://www.coindesk.com/research)\\n*   Consensus 2026 \\n*   Data & Indices \\n*   [Sponsored](https://www.coindesk.com/sponsored-content)\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\nen\\n\\n[CoinDesk 20$2,078.41 0.91%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/cd20)[Bitcoin$77,327.70 1.69%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/bitcoin)[Ethereum$2,283.80 1.15%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/ethereum)[XRP$1.38 0.56%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/xrp)[Solana$83.96 1.17%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/solana)\\n\\n[![Image 1](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/s3y3vcno/production/e3ccf2c7dfe53a58a3fb077817dc4e9394cf9ecc-119x66.png?auto=format) Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Register now](https://consensus.coindesk.com/register)\\n\\n[Policy](https://www.coindesk.com/policy)\\n\\nShare\\n\\nShare this article\\n\\nCopy link[X (Twitter)](https://x.com/intent/tweet?utm_source=twitter&text=Bithumb+scores+a+legal+win+in+South+Korea+as+six-month+suspension+is+lifted+by+local+judge+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge+via+%40coindesk&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?utm_source=linkedin&mini=true&summary=South+Korea%27s+financial+watchdog+imposed+a+%2424.6+million+fine+on+Bithumb+and+partial+suspension+that+came+into+effect+last+month.&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?utm_source=facebook&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Email](mailto:%20?subject=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%20%E2%80%94%20CoinDesk&body=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%0ASouth%20Korea's%20financial%20watchdog%20imposed%20a%20%2424.6%20million%20fine%20on%20Bithumb%20and%20partial%20suspension%20that%20came%20into%20effect%20last%20month.%0A%0ARead%20the%20full%20article%20on%20CoinDesk%3A%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge)\\n\\n# Bithumb scores a legal win in South Korea as six-month suspension is lifted by local judge\\n\\n## South Korea's financial watchdog imposed a $24.6 million fine on Bithumb and partial suspension that came into effect last month.\\n\\nBy[Olivier Acuna](https://www.coindesk.com/author/olivier-acuna)|Edited by[Nikhilesh De](https://www.coindesk.com/author/nikhilesh-de)\\n\\nMay 1, 2026, 7:41 a.m. 2 min read\\n\\n[Make preferred on](https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=coindesk.com)\\n\\n![Image 2: Bithumb](https://www.coindesk.com/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.sanity.io%2Fimages%2Fs3y3vcno%2Fproduction%2F2e7d334bb1f703ff5b0643840f44918d12dc05cc-1500x837.jpg%3Fauto%3Dformat&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\nBithumb scored a win in court against South Korea's financial watchdog by getting its six-month suspension dismissed. (CoinDesk)\\n\\n#### What to know:\\n\\n*   A South Korean court has overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb, one of the country\\u2019s largest cryptocurrency exchanges, while leaving unclear whether a $24.6 million fine is also on hold.\\n*   Regulators had accused Bithumb of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block transactions that should have been stopped.\\n*   The ruling comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny of South Korea\\u2019s crypto sector, including a new data-sharing probe into Bithumb, Upbit and other platforms, and follows Bithumb\\u2019s recent mistaken distribution of billions of dollars\\u2019 worth of bitcoin to users.\\n\\nA South Korean court overturned Bithumb\\u2019s six-month partial business suspension Thursday, [according to Yonhap News](https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20260430139100002?input=1195m).\\n\\nThe news agency cited legal sources, saying that the 2nd Administrative Division of the Seoul Administrative Court\\u2019s Judge Gong Hyeon-jin\\n\\nTitle: South K\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/brazil_ban_analysis.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Brazil Bans Crypto Prediction Markets\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/brazil_ban_analysis.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Brazil prediction markets ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/brazil_ban_analysis.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/brazil_ban_analysis.json:21:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Brazilian authorities have moved to shut down 27 prediction market platforms, including Kalshi and Polymarket. The decision, announced Friday, follows a directive from the Ministry of Finance and enforcement by the National Telecommunications Agency (Anatel), according to state-owned news outlet Agência Brasil. Authorities claimed that such services fall outside Brazil’s current legal framework and therefore operate illegally. “We have been monitoring the evolution of this sector in Brazil, which suffered a period of anarchy because there were no rules, no oversight, from 2018 to 2022,” Finance Ministry executive secretary Dario Durigan reportedly said during a press conference at the Palácio do Planalto. The crackdown follows Resolution 5.298 issued by Brazil’s National Monetary Council (CMN) on Friday, which takes effect in early May and sharply limits what prediction market platforms can offer. Under the new rules, contracts tied to sports, politics, entertainment, or social events are banned, as authorities consider them closer to gambling than financial investments. Only contracts linked to economic indicators, such as inflation, interest rates, exchange rates, or commodity prices, will remain allowed and fall under financial market oversight. Durigan claimed that prediction markets could deepen household debt and expose users to financial harm. A growing number of jurisdictions have moved to ban prediction markets, often folding them into gambling or financial regulations. Several European nations, including France, Belgium and the Netherlands, have blocked or penalized platforms operating without authorization. In the United States, the situation is more fragmented, with an ongoing tug-of-war between federal regulators and individual states over prediction markets.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_report.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Canada Proposes Crypto ATM Ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_report.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Canada crypto ATM ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_report.json:7:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\"The Canadian government has proposed banning Bitcoin and other crypto ATMs.\", \"The government argues the machines are a primary method for scammers and money launderers.\", \"Canada was the site of the worlds first Bitcoin ATM in 2013.\", \"Canada accounts for 10.1% of global crypto ATMs, second only to the United States.\"],\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_report.json:8:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/kelpdao_fallout.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United to Contain KelpDAO Fallout\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/kelpdao_fallout.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/kelpdao_fallout.json:11:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/kelpdao_fallout.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether tied to the Kelp DAO attack and to direct those funds to “DeFi United,” a fund aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council moved to freeze 30,765 Ether (ETH) held in a wallet connected to the $293 million Kelp exploit. In a proposal posted Saturday on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs said directing those funds to a planned remediation effort would “restore normal conditions for Arbitrum users” and the wider ecosystem and that the Ether on Arbitrum “represents a material contribution” toward restoring the Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) token. The submission was made with the support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi and Compound, four of the several crypto protocols affected by the hack. The proposal comes days after Aave Labs and others set up the “DeFi United” on Friday in an effort to fully restore the backing of rsETH. Dune Analytics data shows that about $21 million in contributions has already been made, with contributions including those from Aave Labs CEO Stani Kulechov, Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, Web3 development platform BGD Labs and Babylon, a Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol. Another $215 million has been pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi and Lido to assist the recovery effort, which are subject to governance votes. LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation and Frax Finance have also signaled their intention to help. Aave was hit hard by the Kelp DAO exploit, with its total value locked falling nearly $12 billion in a week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on its lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving more than $190 million in bad debt and triggering a wave of withdrawals. In the Arbitrum proposal, Aave Labs said a full recovery would not only restore rsETH’s backing but also normalize conditions for its holders, liquidity providers and borrowers on Arbitrum and across the broader DeFi ecosystem. Even a “partial recovery would still meaningfully reduce the shortfall,” Aave Labs added. Aave Labs has specifically asked for the 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO and blockchain security platform Certora. Aave Labs said it expects the effort to restore rsETH and compensate its holders to take about 49 days and that it would return the funds if the recovery effort falls through.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_deep_dive.json:3:  \"topic_theme\": \"Canada Proposes Ban on Crypto ATMs\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_deep_dive.json:4:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Canada crypto ATM ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_deep_dive.json:14:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_deep_dive.json:23:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/04/29/canada-proposes-ban-on-bitcoin-atms-as-fraud-cases-mount\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nCanada’s Liberal government has proposed a nationwide ban on bitcoin and other crypto ATMs as part of a broader effort to combat fraud and money laundering. Officials say crypto ATMs have become a “primary method” for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to launder illicit cash, citing findings from the financial intelligence agency FINTRAC. The move comes as lawmakers also weigh banning crypto as a form of electoral donations, even though Canada hosted the world’s first bitcoin ATM in Vancouver in 2013. The measure, included in the Liberal government's Spring Economic Update released Tuesday, would eliminate crypto ATMs nationwide. Officials described the machines as a 'primary method' for defrauding victims and laundering illicit funds. 'To protect Canadians by shutting down a primary method for scammers to defraud victims, and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,' the government said, it plans to prohibit the machines entirely. A crypto ATM (automated teller machine) may sound similar to a traditional cash machine that dispenses money from your bank account, but it works very differently. Instead of withdrawing cash, these machines let users convert physical cash into crypto.\\n\\nTitle: Canada Proposes Crypto ATM Ban to Tackle Scams, Money Laundering\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:17:25 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Canadian government has proposed banning Bitcoin and other crypto ATMs, arguing the machines have become a primary on-ramp for fraudsters and money launderers rather than a convenient access point for everyday users. The government's Spring Economic Update 2026, published on April 28, says crypto ATMs are a “primary method for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,” and explicitly states that the government “proposes to ban crypto ATMs.” The proposal states that Canadians will still be able to buy virtual currencies from brick-and-mortar money services businesses, but the standalone kiosks that have proliferated in malls, gas stations and corner stores would be phased out. The move adds to a broader push by Ottawa to clamp down on what it frames as retail-facing crypto risks as fraud cases surge, while bringing more of the digital asset sector under tighter federal oversight. Authorities say the move is aimed at cutting off one of the most common channels used in scams that have increasingly targeted Canadians. The policy is of particular note given Canada’s early role in the sector. The world’s first publicly available Bitcoin ATM went live in a Vancouver coffee shop in 2013, making Canada the birthplace of the Bitcoin ATM. Since then, the country has grown into one of the most crypto-ATM-dense markets globally, a status regulators say has given it disproportionate exposure to fraud. Coin ATM Radar data estimates that Canada accounts for 10.1% of global crypto ATMs, second only to the United States. A months-long CBC investigation and internal Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (FINTRAC) analysis posted April 28 found that crypto ATMs have become the principal method used by domestic and foreign criminal fraudsters to extract money from Canadian scam victims and push those funds into the crypto ecosystem. Law enforcement agencies told CBC they have seen a clear uptick in cases where victims are instructed to feed cash into these machines under the guise of paying tax debts, securing romance relationships or recovering hacked accounts. The proposed ATM ban sits within a broader effort to tighten controls around high-risk corners of Canada’s crypto market while drawing core infrastructure more firmly into the regulatory perimeter. The same Spring Economic Update bolsters a new Financial Crimes Agency and gives FINTRAC more tools to refuse or revoke registrations for non-compliant money services businesses, including crypto companies.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single-topic.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave-linked DeFi United unveils rsETH recovery plan after $293M Kelp exploit\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single-topic.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United rsETH recovery\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single-topic.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/single-topic.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Aave-Linked DeFi United Details rsETH Recovery Plan\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-linked-defi-united-outlines-plan-to-restore-rseth-backing-after-293m-exploit\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:54:26 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Aave-linked recovery group DeFi United has published a technical implementation plan to restore rsETH backing after the April 18 Kelp bridge exploit released 116,500 rsETH, worth about $293 million at the time, without a corresponding burn on Unichain.\\n\\nThe plan would [convert](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413) committed Ether (ETH) into rsETH in tranches and deposit the tokens into the affected bridge lockbox, allowing the bridge to resume normal operations once the backing is restored. LayerZero and Kelp have also implemented additional security measures before the bridge returns to full operation, according to Aave.\\n\\nIn parallel, DeFi United plans to clear attacker-linked positions across Aave and Compound to recover collateral and resolve market impairments caused by the exploit. The group said seven addresses associated with the exploiter still hold active rsETH-backed positions on Aave and Compound, representing about 107,000 rsETH of the original 116,500 rsETH released in the incident.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Kelp restaking platform exploited, $293M drained in attack**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/restaking-platform-kelp-exploited-293-million)\\n\\nThe proposed sequence would temporarily adjust the rsETH oracle price to enable controlled liquidations, transfer recovered collateral to a DeFi United multisig, restore the oracle, redeem the rsETH for ETH and use the resulting funds to clear deficits across affected markets.\\n\\nThe recovery plan moves the rsETH effort from pledges and public commitments into a coordinated technical process that depends on governance approvals, temporary oracle changes and execution across several DeFi protocols. While the process is designed to restore rsETH backing, it remains contingent on DAO votes, finalized agreements and the attacker not disrupting the liquidation steps.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=802,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-17.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Aave_](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413)\\n\\n## Ethereum backers joined the recovery effort\\n\\nThe technical plan follows earlier efforts to secure funding and governance support for the rsETH recovery.\\n\\nOn Monday, Consensys and Ethereum co-founder Joe Lubin [had joined DeFi United](https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-backers-commit-up-to-30000-eth-to-rseth-recovery-after-bridge-incident) with a commitment of up to 30,000 ETH, while Sharplink, a publicly traded Ethereum treasury company, joined in an advisory role to help structure the recovery plan.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Crypto protocols pledge 43K ETH to restore rsETH backing**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-ecosystem-unites-and-pledges-to-rseth-relief-effort)\\n\\nOn the same day, Aave Labs [had asked the Arbitrum DAO](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united) to release 30,765 ETH frozen by the Arbitrum Security Council [after the exploit](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-freezes-71m-ether-connected-kelp-exploit) and send the funds to DeFi United.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-18.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_DeFi United secured over $300 million in commitments. Source: DeFi United_\\n\\nAs of Tuesday, the DeFi United website [showed](https://defiunited.world/) $302.26 million in total raised or committed toward the recovery effort, equal to 132,706.903 ETH, though some commitments remain subject to DAO votes and final execution.\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**AI-driven hacks could kill DeFi — unless projects act now**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/exploits-uncovered-by-ai-could-kill-defi-unless-projects-act-now/)\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to independent, transparent journalism. This news article is produced in accordance with Cointelegraph’s [Editorial Policy](https://cointelegraph.com/editorial-policy) and aims to provide accurate and timely information. Readers are encouraged to verify information independently.\\nTitle: Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/365847/aave-compound-unveil-technical-plan-to-address-fallout-from-290m-kelp-dao-hack\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-28T17:36:01\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack - Decrypt\\n\\n[![Image 1: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-black.svg)![Image 2: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-white.svg)](https://decrypt.co/)[](https://decrypt.co/gg)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/emerge)\\n\\n[![Image 3: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-white.svg@webp)![Image 4: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-black.svg@webp)](https://decrypt.co/)\\n\\n[News](https://decrypt.co/news)[Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[GG](https://decrypt.co/gg)[Emerge](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[Videos](https://decrypt.co/videos)[Newsletters](https://decrypt.co/newsletters)\\n\\nEnglish\\n\\nSign Up[Partner with us](https://dastan.co/partner)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n[![Image 5: News](blob:http://localhost/0aa0a8ee08caf3bcc8e7e488283150b2)![Image 6: News](blob:http://localhost/9a89213175e2fb47d512c1624a349836)News](https://decrypt.co/news)[![Image 7: Predict](blob:http://localhost/83e225a6c9ce2bac8adf311c3e67de6b)![Image 8: Predict](blob:http://localhost/d3717f8b551ce4e2a9b35e1641d61392)Predict](https://myriad.markets/?utm_source=decrypt&utm_campaign=navbar)[![Image 9: AI](blob:http://localhost/62ceb084dde83843d9887bdc1213ad1f)![Image 10: AI](blob:http://localhost/7aa2f6422d5e2e5af6a262ad86bf9b91)AI](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[![Image 11: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)![Image 12: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[![Image 13: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/e44cea5a102a4ce9cbe1c97f51994f1b)![Image 14: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/f89fd6ac9ca89f35ed6d49f4a70a6652)Gaming](https://decrypt.co/gg)\\n\\n## Coin Prices\\n\\n### [BTC](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin)\\n\\n$77,727.00\\n\\n1.54%\\n### [ETH](https://decrypt.co/price/ethereum)\\n\\n$2,341.28\\n\\n2.55%\\n### [XRP](https://decrypt.co/price/xrp)\\n\\n$1.40\\n\\n1.12%\\n### [BNB](https://decrypt.co/price/binance-coin)\\n\\n$628.90\\n\\n0.93%\\n### [USDC](https://decrypt.co/price/usd-coin)\\n\\n$0.999869\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [SOL](https://decrypt.co/price/solana)\\n\\n$85.36\\n\\n1.96%\\n### [TRX](https://decrypt.co/price/tron)\\n\\n$0.323283\\n\\n0.03%\\n### [FIGR_HELOC](https://decrypt.co/price/figure-heloc)\\n\\n$1.033\\n\\n0.29%\\n### [DOGE](https://decrypt.co/price/dogecoin)\\n\\n$0.109735\\n\\n10.44%\\n### [WBT](https://decrypt.co/price/whitebit)\\n\\n$55.07\\n\\n1.66%\\n### [USDS](https://decrypt.co/price/usds)\\n\\n$0.999764\\n\\n-0.01%\\n### [HYPE](https://decrypt.co/price/hyperliquid)\\n\\n$40.62\\n\\n0.81%\\n### [LEO](https://decrypt.co/price/bitfinex)\\n\\n$10.36\\n\\n-0.03%\\n### [ADA](https://decrypt.co/price/cardano)\\n\\n$0.253118\\n\\n2.82%\\n### [BCH](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin-cash)\\n\\n$455.07\\n\\n1.72%\\n### [XMR](https://decrypt.co/price/monero)\\n\\n$382.36\\n\\n1.02%\\n### [LINK](https://decrypt.co/price/chainlink)\\n\\n$9.40\\n\\n1.76%\\n### [CC](https://decrypt.co/price/canton-network)\\n\\n$0.150786\\n\\n1.15%\\n### [ZEC](https://decrypt.co/price/zcash)\\n\\n$334.99\\n\\n-0.35%\\n### [XLM](https://decrypt.co/price/stellar)\\n\\n$0.164259\\n\\n0.33%\\n### [M](https://decrypt.co/price/memecore)\\n\\n$3.55\\n\\n1.27%\\n### [USD1](https://decrypt.co/price/usd1-wlfi)\\n\\n$0.999547\\n\\n-0.04%\\n### [LTC](https://decrypt.co/price/litecoin)\\n\\n$57.56\\n\\n4.38%\\n### [AVAX](https://decrypt.co/price/avalanche)\\n\\n$9.42\\n\\n2.74%\\n### [HBAR](https://decrypt.co/price/hedera-hashgraph)\\n\\n$0.090681\\n\\n2.00%\\n### [SHIB](https://decrypt.co/price/shiba-inu)\\n\\n$0.00000651\\n\\n6.32%\\n### [USDE](https://decrypt.co/price/ethena-usde)\\n\\n$0.999229\\n\\n0.01%\\n### [SUI](https://decrypt.co/price/sui)\\n\\n$0.936234\\n\\n1.26%\\n### [RAIN](https://decrypt.co/price/rain)\\n\\n$0.00745332\\n\\n1.39%\\n### [PYUSD](https://decrypt.co/price/paypal-usd)\\n\\n$0.999983\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [TON](https://decrypt.co/price/the-open-network)\\n\\n$1.32\\n\\n1.48%\\n### [CRO](https://decrypt.co/price/crypto-com)\\n\\n$0.069339\\n\\n0.09%\\n### [USYC](https://decrypt.co/price/hashnote-usyc)\\n\\n$1.12\\n\\n-0.00%\\n### [XAUT](https://decrypt.co/price/tether-gold)\\n\\n$4,561.39\\n\\n-0.97%\\n### [TAO](https://decrypt.co/price/bittensor)\\n\\n$261.44\\n\\n5.16%\\n### [USDG](https://decrypt.co/price/global-dollar)\\n\\n$0.999782\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [WLFI](https://decrypt.co/price/world-liberty-financial)\\n\\n$0.07344\\n\\n0.47%\\n### [BUIDL](https://decrypt.co/price/blackrock-usd-institutional-digital-liquidity-fund)\\n\\n$1.00\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [PAXG](https://decrypt.co/price/pax-gold)\\n\\n$4,556.28\\n\\n-1.04%\\n### [MNT](https://decrypt.co/price/mantle)\\n\\n$0.639825\\n\\n1.20%\\n### [DOT](h\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_output.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin Price Correction Risk\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_output.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bitcoin futures rally\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_output.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_output.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/result.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"U.S. Senate Bans Itself from Using Prediction Markets\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/result.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Senate Custom Prediction Market Ban\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/result.json:15:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/result.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Acting on a simple, 14-line resolution pushed by Ohio Republican Senator Bernie Moreno, the Senate agreed unanimously to put a restriction between members and the increasingly popular, controversial betting platforms that have drawn scrutiny over insider-trading activity and fights over who has regulatory jurisdiction. “United States Senators have no business engaging in speculative activities like prediction markets while collecting a taxpayer-funded paycheck, period,” said Senator Moreno. The US Senate on Thursday unanimously approved a resolution banning its members and staff, who are often exposed to sensitive information, from using prediction markets. The resolution, passed by unanimous consent, changed the Senate's rules and took immediate effect. “Engaging in any way in a prediction market or trying to place bets where we might have inside information deteriorates the confidence that our constituents have in us,” Republican Senator Bernie Moreno, who introduced the resolution, said on the Senate floor. “By changing the standing rules of the Senate, what we’re doing is allowing our constituents to know, once and for all, that no member of the United States Senate, no member of the staff of the United States Senate, can ever use that inside information as a way to monetize this job whatsoever,” he added. The resolution comes after a special forces soldier involved in the plan to capture former Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro was charged last week, on April 23, with using classified information to make bets on Polymarket, as lawmakers also air concerns over well-timed bets on the Iran war. Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer said on the Senate floor that “of all the issues we debate in Washington, this falls clearly in the category of a ‘no-brainer.’” “We must never allow Congress to turn into a casino where members representing the public can gamble on wars, or economic crises, or elections,” he said. “We should go further; this is a good start, but not enough,” Schumer said. “The administration and its employees must apply these very same rules too, particularly this administration, which shows such a troubling affinity to corruption and self-dealing.” Republican Representative Ashley Hinson posted to X that she would introduce a similar resolution to ban the use of prediction markets in the House. Polymarket posted on X that it fully supported the Senate resolution and its terms of service “already prohibit such conduct, but codifying this into law is a step forward for the industry.” Tarek Mansour, co-founder and CEO of rival prediction market platform Kalshi, also celebrated the resolution in a post on X, adding that it “already proactively blocks members of Congress and enforces against insider trading.”\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json:3:  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin's April Rally Driven by Speculation, Posing Risk of Price Correction\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json:4:  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bitcoin price correction\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json:14:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\\n\\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\\n\\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\\n\\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a report on Thursday.\\n\\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\\n\\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\\n\\nBitcoin is trading around $77,000 at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\\n\\nThe recent surge in Bitcoin’s price, which saw it climb impressively throughout April, may not be as stable as it appears. Market analysts are pointing to underlying data that suggests the rally was built on speculative trading rather than solid, fundamental demand. Experts from analytics firm CryptoQuant have highlighted that the growth was predominantly fueled by perpetual futures contracts, a form of derivative trading that allows for high leverage. Simultaneously, on-chain data shows that actual spot-market buying—the direct purchase of Bitcoin—has been declining. This is a concerning divergence. When prices rise without the backing of genuine buying interest from long-term holders or new retail investors, it often creates a fragile market susceptible to sharp corrections. Historically, such patterns have often been the precursor to significant price drops, as the speculative fervor dies down and the lack of foundational support becomes apparent. While Bitcoin currently holds a strong position near its recent highs, investors are being warned to proceed with caution, as the shaky ground on which the April surge was built could give way, potentially leading to a market-wide crash.\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:109:  \"topic_theme\": \"The core topic (e.g., Bitcoin ETF Inflows Surge)\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:110:  \"primary_keyword\": \"A suggested 2-3 word SEO keyword based on the topic\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:113:  \"chart_coin\": \"The CoinGecko coin id for the primary asset, e.g. bitcoin, ethereum, solana\",\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:122:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:127:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Combine the raw scraped text from all the articles into one large string...\"\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:131:**Tweet quotes:** Do not invent tweets in JSON. The orchestrator runs `extract_tweet_quotes.py` on `aggregated_raw_content` to pull verified quotes from `x.com/status/...` links already present in the news articles. You may include `\"tweet_quotes\": []` as a placeholder; the pipeline fills verified entries after your file is written.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:133:**Do NOT append anything after the closing `}`. The `chart_coin` field inside the JSON replaces the old separate CHART_COIN line.**\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:139:- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:142:- Never fabricate X/Twitter posts or tweet URLs. If articles link to `x.com/.../status/...`, include those URLs in `aggregated_raw_content`; do not make up tweet text.\n/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:143:- `primary_keyword`, `primary_asset`, and `chart_coin` in your JSON are derived from the **chosen story**, not from the RSS search keywords. Use the correct CoinGecko id for the main asset (e.g. `ethereum`, `solana`, `bitcoin`, `ripple` for XRP).\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:3:  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:13:  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/raw.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779352149690}}
